emoji: 🍺
name: Homebrew
group: helper
what: The package manager several tweaks install their programs with, into `/home/linuxbrew`.
why: SteamOS's system partition is read-only and wiped by updates; Homebrew installs outside it. Other tweaks offer to install it when needed; this row shows it and installs it up front.
changes: `/home/linuxbrew`
access: **Needs sudo once** to create that folder
survives-updates: Yes (it lives in /home/linuxbrew)
undo: Not removed automatically (other tweaks' programs live in it); `./install.sh uninstall homebrew` prints Homebrew's own uninstaller
